{
  "initial_instruction": "부족한 구현도 진행해달라는 요청. 앞선 다중 CLI 데스크톱 supervisor MVP에서 빠진 실제 세션 실행, stdin/defer/cancel, 소스 편집 기능을 안전한 범위 안에서 더 구현해야 한다.",
  "result_summary": "Extended the installable desktop MVP from adapter health checks into a bounded pipe-session and scoped source editor slice. Tauri now exposes allowlisted CLI session start, poll, stdin, defer, cancel, and session listing commands for Claude Code CLI, Gemini CLI, Codex CLI, and OpenCode, with workspace-scoped working directories, bounded prompt/stdin/output sizes, timeout cleanup, and resource cancellation. Defer now sends a safe stdin message and appends detected question-like output to `_ops/coordination/human-decision-inbox.json` with blocked-work and resume-action metadata. Tauri also exposes workspace-scoped text file read/write with `_private` and path escape blocking plus project-local backup creation. Workspace Monitor's Desktop tab now has a CLI Session console and Source Editing panel wired to the Tauri bridge, with browser fallback behavior and decision inbox item counts. Requirements, specs, validation, traceability, research, web-search, timing, request trace, and close-out records were updated. PTY/xterm.js, Monaco, autonomous source-affecting agent execution, Tauri shell sidecars, Rust/Tauri compile, and installed CLI smoke tests remain follow-up work.",
  "work_mode": "governance",
